          "source_text_sha256": "6f9030d7ff6d8f72887b59e40dba14a781a833112275a72e3b15403f93b0db43",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On March 7, 2015 at 00:05, a witness observed in the sky, while driving, a group of 9 red lights above a nearby hill. The lights appeared to move silently and quickly in formation. The witness stopped to take photos, then, upon returning home, continued observing with his family until the phenomenon disappeared. The hypothesis of Thai lanterns is entirely consistent with the observation: these objects are inherently dim (equivalent to a small garden torch) and therefore often perceived farther away than they actually are, thus appearing larger and faster than they truly are; the wind, though weak, was far from zero. It's common to feel nothing on the ground. Friday night parties are, of course, less frequent than Saturday ones, but they still occur (often professional or association-related parties, for example, and it's also carnival season). The witness photo No. 1164 is entirely consistent with a photo of Thai lanterns. The southeast wind: 9 to 28 km/h is consistent with the observed movement in the direction of Guermentes towards Chelles. See the weather report at Roissy. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B,\" probable observation of Thai lanterns.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "9b5fe81e6d2d2be2cb9bf9b6d2356dfa95689e12bcedce9f01140b4492a319fd"
        }
